                       (Font.TS.panel, web "section-title"); web t('telemetry.energyCharging').
      * MetricCard  -> TSMetricCard x2 (Charger Voltage "V" / Charger Current "A"),
                       locale number + invariant unit caption.
      * rows        -> Charger Power, Energy Added, Battery Level, Charge Rate (Zap glyph),
                       muted label + monospaced value, em-dash on null (web `!= null ? : '—'`).
      * state pill  -> EnergyChargingStateChip: Charging->statusInfo (web cyan),
                       Complete->statusSuccess (web green), other/nil->textMuted (web gray);
                       text = raw state or t('common.unknown') (web parity).
  - PARITY QUIRK reproduced verbatim (NOT a native "fix" — Honesty rule 5/9): the web
    renders the SI watt value charger_power_w via fmtWithUnit(value,'kW') and the SI
    watt-hour value charge_energy_added_wh via fmtWithUnit(value,'kWh') WITHOUT rescaling
    the magnitude. EnergyChargingFormat.withUnit reproduces this exactly (7,680.00 kW,
    18,450.00 kWh); pinned by EnergyChargingFormatTests.testWithUnitSpacesValueAndUnitWithoutRescaling.
